<title>GREECE: EUROBANK/INTERBANK CUT LOAN, DEPO RATES.</title>
<headline>EUROBANK/INTERBANK CUT LOAN, DEPO RATES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eurobank-Interbank said on</p>
<p>Thursday they will cut their base lending rate for business</p>
<p>loans by 325 basis points down to 12.5 percent effective June 1.</p>
<p>&quot;The continued fall in inflation led Eurobank and Interbank</p>
<p>to adjust to new market conditions and reduce business loan</p>
<p>rates and mortgages as well as deposit rates,&quot; Eurobank said in</p>
<p>a statement.</p>
<p>Deposit rates will range from 8.0 to 9.75 percent.</p>
<p>Mortgage rates will have as follows:</p>
<p>    ** Five-year fixed			 10.5 percent</p>
<p>    ** Bonus floating rate		   12.0 percent</p>
<p>    ** Floating rate			   14.0 percent</p>
<p>    ** Low start mortgage		     7.0 percent</p>
<p>    ** Floating rate in forex		 5.0 percent</p>
<p>Eurobank bought Interbank from Banque Worms in 1996.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
